      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0041",
      "sequence": 896,
      "meaning": "The warriors on Laṅkā’s battlements resemble clouds seated upon Meru’s peaks. Battle drums and innumerable kettledrums and trumpets sound, rousing champions and splitting cowards’ hearts. The demons look upon the immense companies of huge bears and monkeys, who disregard every difficult ravine, break mountains open for roads, grind their teeth, roar and bite their lips in threat. Cries of Rāvaṇa on one side and Rāma on the other meet as battle begins. Demons topple mountain peaks; monkeys leap, catch them and throw them back.",
