      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0042",
      "sequence": 897,
      "meaning": "Empowered by Rāma, the monkey hosts crush formations of demon champions and climb the fortress everywhere crying victory to the sunlike glory of Raghubīra. Night-rangers flee like clouds driven by a mighty wind; children and distressed women wail and curse Rāvaṇa for summoning death through his rule. Hearing his army waver, the enraged king turns the warriors back, threatening to kill with his dreadful sword anyone who retreats after consuming his wealth. Shamed and frightened, they return angrily, accepting that death facing the foe adorns a hero and abandoning love of life. They challenge and strike the bears and monkeys with many weapons, bars and tridents.",
