    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0043",
      "sequence": 898,
      "meaning": "Terrified monkeys begin to flee, though they will ultimately win. They call for Aṅgada, Hanumān, Nala, Nīla and Dvivida. Hanumān hears his army is distressed while he guards the west gate, where Meghanāda fights and the gate resists. Furious as Death, he roars, leaps upon Laṅkā and charges Indrajit with a mountain. He smashes the chariot and kills the charioteer, then kicks Meghanāda in the chest. Another charioteer finds him senseless and swiftly carries him home. Hearing Hanumān has gone alone atop the fort, battle-bold Aṅgada leaps up as easily as play.",
