    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0044",
      "sequence": 899,
      "meaning": "The two furious monkeys remember Rāma’s power and rush upon Rāvaṇa’s palace proclaiming Kosala’s Lord. They seize and topple it with its finials, frightening Rāvaṇa; women beat their breasts at the arrival of the two troublemakers. Performing monkey antics, they terrify them and proclaim Rāmacandra’s fame, then wrench golden pillars loose and begin further havoc. Roaring, they fall upon the enemy army and crush it with immense arm-strength—one with kicks, another with slaps—telling those who will not worship Rāma to reap this fruit. They twist off heads and throw them before Rāvaṇa like pots of curd bursting.",
