    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0045",
      "sequence": 900,
      "meaning": "Whenever Aṅgada and Hanumān find a great commander, they seize his feet and fling him before Rāma. Vibhīṣaṇa names each, and Rāma grants even those wicked man-eaters his own abode—the final state yogis seek—because the tender-hearted ocean of compassion is remembered even in hostility. Śiva asks Bhavānī what other Lord is so gracious; utterly unfortunate are the dull who hear this and still do not worship him. Aṅgada and Hanumān penetrate the fortress like two Mandara mountains churning the sea. After pulverizing the enemy army until sunset, the tireless pair leap back to the Lord.",
