      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0046",
      "sequence": 901,
      "meaning": "The two bow at Rāma’s lotus feet; pleased, he looks graciously upon them and their weariness vanishes. Knowing they have returned, many bear and monkey warriors come back. At dusk the night-rangers gain strength and charge shouting Rāvaṇa’s name; the monkeys turn and the two fierce armies clash without admitting defeat. Black demon heroes and many-coloured monkey faces appear like dense autumn clouds driven by wind. Anīka, Akampana and Atikāya spread an illusion that confuses the army: in an instant utter darkness falls and blood, stones and ash rain down. The monkey army panics, unable to see one another.",
