    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0047",
      "sequence": 902,
      "meaning": "Rāma knows the entire secret and summons Aṅgada and Hanumān, explains events, and the elephant-like monkeys charge in anger. Smiling, the compassionate Lord strings his bow and instantly releases a fire-arrow. Light appears and darkness vanishes as doubt leaves at the rise of knowledge. Bears and monkeys regain strength, joy and courage; Hanumān and Aṅgada roar, and night-rangers flee at their challenge. The bears and monkeys seize the fugitives, dash them on the ground or throw them into the sea where crocodiles, serpents and fish devour them. Some die, some are wounded and some escape into the fort as the roaring army shatters enemy strength.",
