      "meaning": "At night the four monkey armies return to Rāma; one merciful glance removes their exhaustion. Rāvaṇa summons his ministers and reports that monkeys have destroyed half the army. His aged maternal great-uncle and chief minister Mālyavān offers pure policy: since Sītā’s abduction, indescribable omens have appeared, and none opposed to Rāma—whose fame Veda and Purāṇa sing—has found happiness. The very compassionate Lord who killed mighty Hiraṇyākṣa, Madhu and Kaiṭabha has descended. Why oppose the form of Time, fire to the forest of villains, treasury of virtue and mass of wisdom, whom Śiva and Brahmā serve?",
