      "meaning": "Mālyavān urges Rāvaṇa to abandon enmity, return Vaidehī and worship the supremely loving Lord. The advice strikes like arrows. Rāvaṇa darkens and expels the unlucky old man, saying he would kill him if not aged. Mālyavān leaves, thinking the compassionate Lord intends Rāvaṇa’s death. Indrajit angrily promises that his prowess will be seen at dawn and needs few words. Reassured, Rāvaṇa seats his son affectionately. At daybreak monkeys again attack the four gates, besiege the inaccessible fort and throw down mountain peaks as armed demons rush out.",
